1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,660
Ah, I see. I can't enter Kamihama because Alina Gray has the whole city covered by a magical barrier.

2
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:14,280
Oh well. I have a good idea of what's going on in there.

3
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:21,720
You magical girls must have figured out how to use the doppel effect that occurs in the barrier to keep yourselves from turning into witches.

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:27,200
You're right about one thing. You're not obligated to become witches.

5
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:39,600
But not only are you wasting your precious souls trying to escape your fate as magical girls, you have no problem if your actions harm all of humankind in the process.

6
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,460
Honestly, I don't understand you.

7
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:24,670
You've created a truly magnificent piece of art!

8
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:30,050
I was getting so bored playing with these goody-goody girls and their niente souls.

9
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:34,870
Your next piece will be even more high-class and filled with emotiva.

10
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:37,870
At least that's what I'm hoping for.

11
00:02:43,990 --> 00:02:55,030
Where is Walpurgis knocked now?

12
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:59,470
Still on course. She's heading straight for Mitakihara at the same speed.

13
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:01,770
You think we can catch up to her?

14
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:04,830
It'll be close, but we'll make it in time.

15
00:03:05,470 --> 00:03:06,490
Then let's go.

16
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:08,910
For the future of Magical Girls!

17
00:03:09,350 --> 00:03:11,830
And for our big sis, Iroha.

18
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,630
Your insane plan!

19
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:15,490
Is the last thing she'd want!

20
00:03:15,950 --> 00:03:18,670
Stop this! You have no idea what you're doing!

21
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:24,870
We calculated all the risks, actually.

22
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:29,750
For example, right now, we're at less than 1% of our total estimated casualties.

23
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:31,610
You are insane!

24
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:36,870
Two huge witches fusing has the same effect as two black holes fusing.

25
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:44,250
We estimate that when Embryo Eve absorbs Walpurgis knocked, it will create a massive shockwave of energy.

26
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:56,370
But with our new system in place, Magical Girls won't ever become witches again.

27
00:03:56,370 --> 00:04:08,450
Yachiyo, what's going on? What is that?

28
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:12,890
If we can change things, it's our duty to change them.

29
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:17,110
You're seeing Ui's wish, Toka's wish, and mine.

30
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:19,810
This is our three wishes fulfilled.

31
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:24,190
As for Iroha, we put her someplace safe till this is over.

32
00:04:24,570 --> 00:04:25,650
So don't you worry!

33
00:04:26,110 --> 00:04:28,450
You should find somewhere safe to hide, too.

34
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:38,170
Originally, the universe was fated to end in the future, from heat death.

35
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:42,510
Luckily, my kind found a way to extend its lifespan.

36
00:04:42,510 --> 00:05:06,370
During puberty, when the hope a young human girl possesses shifts into despair, it creates a massive amount of energy.

37
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:11,910
It's miraculous emotional energy, strong enough to hold back the tides of entropy.

38
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:15,110
All of you are incredibly valuable.

39
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:18,710
You're the key to extending the lifespan of the universe, after all.

40
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:25,370
And if you really think about the conditions of the contracts you made with me, why, they're in your favor.

41
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:28,650
That's how a Magical Girl's contract works.

42
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:36,150
I don't agree with what the Magiists claim, that the fate of a Magical Girl is tragic.

43
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:42,030
Becoming a witch isn't just the price you have to pay for the miracle you asked for.

44
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:46,750
It's your contribution to the survival of your species and the universe.

45
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:50,710
Think about it.

46
00:05:51,030 --> 00:05:55,230
The future of the human race and the universe, or the end of it all.

47
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:56,970
Which would you choose?

48
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:59,890
I think it's obvious, don't you?

49
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:03,330
You, who've become Magical Girls.

50
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:09,350
It's my room.

51
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:12,050
How did I get back here?

52
00:06:12,050 --> 00:06:16,390
I remember getting sealed in the teeny Q-bay by Nemu.

53
00:06:16,770 --> 00:06:17,930
What's going on?

54
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,190
That's...

55
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,110
Yup.

56
00:06:25,590 --> 00:06:26,230
Ui!

57
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:29,490
Oh, Ui, it's you!

58
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:30,690
It's you!

59
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:33,450
I missed you so much!

60
00:06:33,450 --> 00:06:35,210
I missed you too, sis.

61
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:36,470
I looked for you.

62
00:06:36,910 --> 00:06:38,390
I looked all over for you.

63
00:06:38,910 --> 00:06:39,970
I know you did.

64
00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:41,290
I know you tried.

65
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:43,910
I swear, I'll never let you go again.

66
00:06:44,470 --> 00:06:46,030
You won't be alone anymore.

67
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,330
I'm sorry, sis.

68
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:51,570
Thanks, but I'm fine.

69
00:06:52,070 --> 00:06:52,450
Huh?

70
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:55,910
Ui...

71
00:06:55,910 --> 00:07:00,010
The day I became a Magical Girl, everything changed.

72
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:01,570
I changed.

73
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:03,730
I'm not me anymore.

74
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:05,250
Of course you are.

75
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:06,090
You're Ui.

76
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:07,290
The real Ui.

77
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:09,410
And I'm your big sis.

78
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,430
I am sorry, sis.

79
00:07:12,090 --> 00:07:13,470
But we messed up.

80
00:07:14,090 --> 00:07:15,650
We felt at everything we wanted.

81
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:18,650
We should have just left things alone, and...

82
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:20,410
In the end, we couldn't save anyone.

83
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:22,650
I'm sorry.

84
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:24,590
I don't care about that!

85
00:07:24,590 --> 00:07:27,170
All I want is for you to be well again and happy.

86
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:28,110
That's it!

87
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,750
That's the only reason I became a Magical Girl!

88
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,310
It's what kept me going!

89
00:07:34,310 --> 00:07:35,910
I know, but...

90
00:07:35,910 --> 00:07:37,350
That's not fair, sis.

91
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:40,090
What about you?

92
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:42,570
I want you to be happy too, you know?

93
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:48,570
I wanted to save you from the fate of Magical Girls.

94
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:51,650
I wanted so much for you to be happy.

95
00:07:51,650 --> 00:07:56,130
Why did everything have to happen the way it did?

96
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:58,130
It's okay, Ui.

97
00:07:58,290 --> 00:08:01,470
I don't know how, but I'll figure out a way to fix all of it.

98
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,150
Please stop us, sis.

99
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,410
Do it for the sake of everyone.

100
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:09,690
Stop Embryo Eve.

101
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:11,910
And Nemu and Touka, too.

102
00:08:11,910 --> 00:08:18,850
I care about you so much, and I want to save you from a Magical Girl's horrible fate.

103
00:08:19,830 --> 00:08:24,850
But if our plan succeeds, you're going to regret not stopping us when you have the chance.

104
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:26,910
So please...

105
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:32,910
But Ui, if I can stop you guys, will that turn you back to normal?

106
00:08:35,870 --> 00:08:37,390
Tell me you'll turn back!

107
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:38,230
Please!

108
00:08:38,230 --> 00:08:44,730
Hang on.

109
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:47,110
I'll find a way to get you out of here.

110
00:08:47,450 --> 00:08:48,690
Why do you look like that?

111
00:08:49,090 --> 00:08:50,150
Come with me, Ui!

112
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:52,270
It's too late for me.

113
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:54,390
But there's others who need your help.

114
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:56,310
So be strong.

115
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:59,610
Because there's a bunch of people whose hands you're going to have to hold.

116
00:09:00,090 --> 00:09:00,770
Stop it!

117
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:02,470
Please, let me see you again!

118
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:03,950
There's no time now.

119
00:09:04,450 --> 00:09:05,490
Your friend needs you.

120
00:09:06,490 --> 00:09:09,590
She's the first of many people you'll have to save when you get back.

121
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:11,090
So go.

122
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:12,550
Help her.

123
00:09:13,190 --> 00:09:13,590
Ui!

124
00:09:13,990 --> 00:09:16,390
I'm sorry I caused so much trouble for you.

125
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:19,010
Thank you for being the best, sis.

126
00:09:19,710 --> 00:09:20,550
I love you.

127
00:09:28,230 --> 00:09:28,830
Ui!

128
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:30,470
Ui!

129
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:39,090
Why are you here, Iroha?

130
00:09:39,730 --> 00:09:40,450
Curly!

131
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:42,290
You shouldn't have come.

132
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:45,110
It's not like there's anything you can do to help.

133
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:46,470
Your doppel's taking over!

134
00:09:46,770 --> 00:09:47,790
Stop using it!

135
00:09:48,270 --> 00:09:49,510
I don't care anymore.

136
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:52,850
Curly!

137
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,890
Don't let your doppel get the tr-

138
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:57,870
Why fight it?

139
00:09:57,870 --> 00:10:00,110
I gave up on everything.

140
00:10:00,730 --> 00:10:01,890
A long time ago.

141
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:03,850
Curly!

142
00:10:10,890 --> 00:10:15,950
On that day, I abandoned everything I was.

143
00:10:16,630 --> 00:10:18,730
Just like I abandoned her.

144
00:10:19,590 --> 00:10:20,990
I gave up.

145
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:50,970
The fate of a magical girl.

146
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:53,070
The fate of a magical girl was a heavier burden than I expected.

147
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:57,990
Which is a really strong, and beating them's hard.

148
00:10:58,590 --> 00:11:01,710
But the only way you can get grief seeds is by beating them.

149
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:08,130
Even though I had all these powers as a magical girl, I couldn't get that strong.

150
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:11,010
I didn't know how long I'd survive like that.

151
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:17,290
But there was a girl who was even weaker than me.

152
00:11:18,290 --> 00:11:19,770
Way, way weaker.

153
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:30,910
Are you okay?

154
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:34,510
Oh my gosh!

155
00:11:34,510 --> 00:11:58,270
Watch out!

156
00:11:58,270 --> 00:12:18,530
I thought I was gonna die in there. Thanks for saving me.

157
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:19,970
Sure.

158
00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:26,570
I don't know you. Are you new?

159
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:29,750
Yes. I don't live around here though.

160
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:35,450
Oh. Well, since you're new and not from here, you're kinda on my turf.

161
00:12:36,810 --> 00:12:40,970
You're supposed to fight the witches in your own area, not the ones in someone else's.

162
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,710
It's one of the rules of this job.

163
00:12:42,710 --> 00:12:50,350
I'm so sorry. I saw the kitty run into the labyrinth and I followed it. I swear, it'll never happen again.

164
00:12:51,430 --> 00:12:54,510
Don't worry about it. This stuff happens sometimes.

165
00:12:54,510 --> 00:12:56,510
Y-you're not mad?

166
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:58,630
Uh-uh. Bye.

167
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:03,950
What?

168
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:11,470
I hate to ask this, but do you have an extra grief seed?

169
00:13:11,470 --> 00:13:20,470
See, my soul gen got pretty tainted after that fight. So, if you had one...

170
00:13:20,470 --> 00:13:30,470
Sorry.

171
00:13:30,470 --> 00:13:38,790
Oh, don't apologize. I mean, who's got extra grief seeds, right? I shouldn't have even asked. It was dumb.

172
00:13:40,390 --> 00:13:46,450
No, it's not. But I don't have any. I'm not strong enough to get any myself.

173
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:49,450
I'm sorry.

174
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:54,990
No, you don't have to apologize. I shouldn't have even asked you. I'm sorry.

175
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,110
Still, I feel bad.

176
00:13:57,850 --> 00:14:02,350
Not even. I was dumb. I should have brought along some extras.

177
00:14:03,230 --> 00:14:09,630
Anyway, thanks again for saving me. I mean it. I hate to think what would have happened to me and the kitty without you.

178
00:14:11,510 --> 00:14:11,990
Sure.

179
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:17,990
I-I'm still new at this, but I promise. I'll work hard and be a great magical girl someday.

180
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:22,230
I'll get enough grief seeds for everyone that no one's gonna run out.

181
00:14:26,050 --> 00:14:28,490
Yeah. Let's do our best.

182
00:14:29,150 --> 00:14:31,870
Yeah! Right. Let's do our best.

183
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:40,770
We never asked each other's names. We didn't even share our contact info, so we could stay in touch.

184
00:14:42,430 --> 00:14:45,610
That was the last time I saw her at that station.

185
00:14:47,150 --> 00:14:49,870
She kept waving at me and didn't stop.

186
00:14:50,830 --> 00:14:53,710
She just kept waving and waving.

187
00:14:53,710 --> 00:14:58,210
She was scared, too.

188
00:14:59,210 --> 00:15:00,790
What would you have done, Iroha?

189
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:03,290
I wonder what happened to her.

190
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:06,170
Did she go and join the Magius?

191
00:15:06,830 --> 00:15:08,290
Is she even still alive?

192
00:15:08,290 --> 00:15:17,190
On that day, I gave up.

193
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:23,450
Instead of helping her, I abandoned her.

194
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:27,590
I'm not like you, Iroha.

195
00:15:27,950 --> 00:15:28,990
Not even close.

196
00:15:30,690 --> 00:15:31,910
Please, go away!

197
00:15:32,330 --> 00:15:34,150
My dad! You have this job!

198
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,210
I could have helped her, but I didn't.

199
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:38,130
I chose not to.

200
00:15:38,470 --> 00:15:39,750
Hang on a little longer!

201
00:15:40,050 --> 00:15:41,530
I'm here! I'll save you!

202
00:15:41,530 --> 00:16:06,590
The idea of what a magical girl should be is a reflection of the ethical values of humans and changes depending on the era.

203
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:11,950
Magical girls have always been considered holy due to their special powers.

204
00:16:12,630 --> 00:16:16,930
The masses want someone to look up to, and magical girls personify that ideal.

205
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:22,950
Throughout your history, my kind has done everything possible to accommodate those desires.

206
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:26,490
But going back to what I was saying about changing values,

207
00:16:26,950 --> 00:16:29,410
in some eras, justice meant saving the weak.

208
00:16:29,770 --> 00:16:34,470
In other eras, it meant eliminating the weak to strengthen society and save it from extinction.

209
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:39,670
You see, the concept of justice, or what you humans believe is right,

210
00:16:40,110 --> 00:16:42,330
changed depending on the era in which you lived.

211
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:46,750
Therefore, your attempt at keeping magical girls from their fate,

212
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:49,430
this temporary salvation you're offering them,

213
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,470
is nothing but a reflection of this era's wave of thinking.

214
00:16:53,990 --> 00:16:57,610
Instead of the Magius' plan, which is based on temporary ideology,

215
00:16:57,610 --> 00:17:02,050
our system, which offers your species' perpetual growth and prosperity,

216
00:17:02,370 --> 00:17:03,930
is much better for you humans.

217
00:17:04,350 --> 00:17:07,430
I can't understand why this is so difficult for you to accept.

218
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:15,270
I'll be honest, Cube, your fuzzy kind's visione missione stir nothing in my cuore.

219
00:17:16,130 --> 00:17:19,430
But the fate you so kindly shared tells me one thing,

220
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:23,530
that our culture and civilization were created by feeding them the souls

221
00:17:23,530 --> 00:17:25,950
of all the magical girls you tricked.

222
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,390
Destroying your kind, Eon Duvere?

223
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:30,030
That goes without saying.

224
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:33,430
But do you know who I think really deserves restituire

225
00:17:33,430 --> 00:17:35,950
for all the years of unfairness and exploitation?

226
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,650
Well, it should be obvious.

227
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:39,650
Or isn't it?

228
00:17:43,370 --> 00:17:46,270
I wasn't strong enough to be part of the Magius.

229
00:17:46,890 --> 00:17:48,910
Or strong enough to be like you.

230
00:17:49,190 --> 00:17:49,890
Shut up!

231
00:17:50,190 --> 00:17:51,590
I couldn't be anything.

232
00:17:52,370 --> 00:17:53,110
I'm nobody.

233
00:17:53,810 --> 00:17:54,730
I'm nothing.

234
00:17:55,210 --> 00:17:56,070
Stop that!

235
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:57,850
I don't care what you say!

236
00:17:58,090 --> 00:17:59,410
I'm going to save you!

237
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:01,950
Yeroha?

238
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:03,570
Kuroi!

239
00:18:03,930 --> 00:18:04,170
Kana!

240
00:18:08,370 --> 00:18:08,930
Kuroi!

241
00:18:10,850 --> 00:18:11,330
Yeroha...

242
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:13,190
With a combined attack,

243
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:15,330
we might be able to break you out of it.

244
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:19,410
But I can't move my body.

245
00:18:19,810 --> 00:18:20,570
Try harder!

246
00:18:21,390 --> 00:18:21,930
I did.

247
00:18:22,110 --> 00:18:22,690
I can't.

248
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:24,410
I'll save you, you hear me?

249
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:25,970
I'll save everyone!

250
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:29,430
No way am I going to let Ui down!

251
00:18:31,090 --> 00:18:33,010
There's no point saving me.

252
00:18:33,670 --> 00:18:34,330
I'm useless.

253
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:35,650
I'm weak.

254
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:37,930
But together, we can be strong.

255
00:18:39,310 --> 00:18:41,510
If it's too hard to get stronger yourself,

256
00:18:41,610 --> 00:18:42,830
we can get strong together!

257
00:18:43,210 --> 00:18:44,490
I don't think I can.

258
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:47,090
No matter how hard things get,

259
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:48,710
as long as someone's there for you,

260
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:49,830
you can face anything!

261
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:54,050
I was scared and weak too,

262
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:56,190
but I had my friends to help me!

263
00:18:57,990 --> 00:18:59,050
But I...

264
00:18:59,050 --> 00:18:59,550
Kuroi!

265
00:18:59,550 --> 00:18:59,590
Kuroi!

266
00:18:59,590 --> 00:19:03,110
Let's do our best!

267
00:19:03,630 --> 00:19:04,150
Right!

268
00:19:04,570 --> 00:19:05,570
Let's do our best!

269
00:19:05,570 --> 00:19:08,930
You had the chance!

270
00:19:08,930 --> 00:19:10,930
Why didn't you do the right thing

271
00:19:10,930 --> 00:19:11,790
and save her?

272
00:19:11,790 --> 00:19:17,150
You had the chance to do the right thing to do with you!

273
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:18,110
Come on!

274
00:19:20,610 --> 00:19:22,050
What's wrong with me?

275
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:24,890
You've been so nice to me.

276
00:19:25,650 --> 00:19:27,150
You've done so much for me.

277
00:19:28,590 --> 00:19:29,150
So...

278
00:19:29,150 --> 00:19:31,310
Why do I feel so pathetic?

279
00:19:33,090 --> 00:19:34,950
I shouldn't have made that wish

280
00:19:34,950 --> 00:19:36,730
or wanted to save anyone.

281
00:19:37,490 --> 00:19:39,270
I should have stayed normal!

282
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:42,250
You can be strong just like me.

283
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:43,790
You're a magical girl.

284
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:47,430
Our strength comes from hopes and wishes, after all.

285
00:19:48,130 --> 00:19:50,990
Don't give up on yourself or your wish.

286
00:19:55,790 --> 00:19:57,990
Kuroi, when you made your wish,

287
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,230
who was it for?

288
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,810
I don't remember.

289
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:03,690
What was it?

290
00:20:06,010 --> 00:20:06,650
Kuroi!

291
00:20:07,250 --> 00:20:09,370
Become a magical girl like me!

292
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:12,870
Hey, Ira...

293
00:20:12,870 --> 00:20:17,870
Tell me...

294
00:20:17,870 --> 00:20:23,430
How long do I have to keep being a magical girl?

295
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:33,550
We just broke through Alina's barrier.

296
00:20:34,450 --> 00:20:34,950
Oh no!

297
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,210
We're outside the doppel system now!

298
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:41,750
It's impossible for me to be...

299
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:44,010
the person I hope to be.

300
00:20:45,570 --> 00:20:47,250
So I thought...

301
00:20:47,250 --> 00:20:48,550
maybe...

302
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:49,730
if I became this,

303
00:20:49,870 --> 00:20:51,230
I'd stop hating myself.

304
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:54,750
And I'd go back to before I met you.

305
00:20:54,750 --> 00:21:13,750
No, no one will save me.

306
00:21:13,750 --> 00:21:18,750
No, I don't need to save anyone.

307
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:22,750
No, I can stop being a magical boy.

308
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:43,750
Oh my God.

309
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:51,750
Now, are you watching those days over here?

310
00:21:51,750 --> 00:22:02,930
I'm sorry, Yui. Your big sister let you down.

